The product invokes the following programs as **separate operating-system processes**. It does
not link against them or incorporate their code.

### yt-dlp

- Project: <https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp>
- Source licence: **The Unlicense**

Windows `yt-dlp.exe` PyInstaller bundles may be **GPLv3+** when downloaded at runtime; see
<https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/blob/master/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt>.

### FFmpeg

- Project: <https://ffmpeg.org/> · Source: <https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg>

| Distribution | Source of the binary | Effective licence |
|---|---|---|
| **Docker image** | Debian `ffmpeg` package (`apt-get install ffmpeg`) | **GPL-2.0-or-later** |
| **Windows** | FFmpeg build downloaded with yt-dlp tooling at runtime | **GPL-2.0-or-later** (typical GPL builds) |

Debian documents that default `ffmpeg` packages are **GPL v2+** when GPL codec libraries are
linked. Corresponding source for the exact Debian packages in a published image can be obtained
with `apt-get source ffmpeg` inside the container, or from **Debian snapshot archives** at
<https://snapshot.debian.org/> for the image's Debian version.

This application launches `ffmpeg` as an external process only; it is not a derivative work of
FFmpeg.

